ve_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123978","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123978","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123978.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123978.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Backports #123955 to 3.x.\r\nImplements https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12555 for 3.x.\r\n\r\nVideo:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e259e1f4-d936-4c82-a1c2-66680966c706\r\n\r\n## UI\r\n3.x has no enclosing game window, so I have added the speed selector to the run / stop etc toolbar on the top right. This is slightly more annoying to use than in 4.x (where the drop down can be part of the extended game window), as changing the game speed changes focus from the game to the editor, but that's an already existing problem with all the debugging functionality I think.\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n* This was fairly simple to do, as I'd already done the lion's share of the work for #123955, and it was a copy paste to backport, so just needed a small UI front end. It would have been rude not to.\r\n* I've made it so the speed selector only shows up while running the game, so as not to clutter the interface.\r\n* Speed is remembered for each time you run the game (but not saved with it).\r\n* I'm not an editor specialist, so any improvement suggestions welcome, I kind of made it up as I went.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123978/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123978/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}